# dendro_fccz4 — NRPy-generated fCCZ4 project for Dendro-GR

GENERATED PROJECT - DO NOT EDIT.
Generator: nrpy.infrastructures.Dendro
Regenerate with: `python -m nrpy.examples.dendro_fccz4 ...`
Module ABI: `$MODULE_ABI_HASH`

## Layout (whitepaper section 12.1)

- `manifest/` — canonical JSON manifests and hashes (module, state,
  parameters, CFunctions, stencils, provenance, file hashes, SHA256SUMS).
- `tools/` — the generated project verifier, the safe Dendro-GR installer,
  and the copy verifier / remover.
- `Dendro-GR/FCCZ4_GR/` — the sibling module installed into a Dendro-GR
  checkout (generated sources, context, pars, tests).

## Verify

    python tools/verify_generated_project.py

## Install (transactional; default is a dry run)

This profile is qualified against the NRPy mock host only.  If the target
Dendro-GR root defines a real `dendro5` target, the module's CMake stops the
configure with a `FATAL_ERROR` rather than compile the mock `ot::Block` /
`DVector` doubles against the real host (whitepaper section 13.2).  Undo an
installation with `python tools/remove_generated_module.py --dendro-root
/path/to/Dendro-GR`.


    python tools/copy_into_dendro.py --dendro-root /path/to/Dendro-GR
    python tools/copy_into_dendro.py --dendro-root /path/to/Dendro-GR --execute --apply-root-cmake-patch

## Status

Dendrolib is UNPINNED in this repository; the generated module builds and
runs against the mock host stubs (the PR 7 mock vehicle).  Algebraic
projection, ADM initial-data conversion, connection initialization and
constraint diagnostics are registered in this profile, and
`manifest/{projection,initial_data,diagnostics}.json` describe the registered
CFunctions.  Real Dendro-GR host integration, physical boundaries and the
checkpoint ABI remain separate qualified profiles; `manifest/boundaries.json`
and `manifest/dendrolib_capabilities.json` are the deferral records.